# Feature Development Process (Mandatory)

Before implementing any new feature, module, page, dashboard, or workspace screen, produce a **Product Design Report** and wait for user approval. Do not write implementation code until approved.

Priority: a coherent enterprise healthcare product — not disconnected CRUD pages.

## Product Design Report (required sections)

1. Business objective  
2. Target user role(s) / workspace(s)  
3. User workflow (step-by-step)  
4. UI wireframe description (layout, primary actions, empty/error states)  
5. Dashboard widgets  
6. KPIs  
7. Navigation impact (sidebar, homepage, shortcuts)  
8. Database changes  
9. Permissions and security  
10. Notifications  
11. Reports and exports  
12. Analytics generated  
13. Mobile responsiveness  
14. Future extensibility  
15. Implementation plan (files/helpers to touch; what is reused vs new)

## After approval

Implement only what the report covers. Fit the work into the role's workspace experience (see role-workspaces rule). Prefer evolving existing code; preserve business logic; share helpers, not identical role UIs.
